        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/c67d28/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-14T21:45:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Do Absolute Zero's enemy movement effects (Adhesive Foam Pellets and Approaching Zero) stay in effect for the rest of the game or just the round? Adhesive Foam Pellets requires an action to do, but reads as a permenant in the text. Approaching Zero is on going and also reads as a permenant as well. Are they? Or are they meant just for the round? or is Adhesive Foam Pellets for the round and Approaching Zero a permenent?&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Card text:</strong></p><p><em>Adhesive Foam Pellets:</em></p><p><strong>Action Required:</strong><em> If a target would be damaged this attack, reduce the target's move value to 1 instead. 4 dice (hits only on 6)</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>Approaching Zero:&nbsp;</em></p><p><strong>Ongoing:</strong> <em>Whenever Absolute Zero Deals damage to a target, reduce that target's move value by 1 for each point of of damage dealt. (Move value cannot be reduced to below 1.)</em></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:42.398Z",
